	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zayTFgjsly8"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """This is part of a crash course in vocabulary that will get you started building your own OWL ontologies. In this video, I present the Web Ontology Language (OWL) terms you need to know, and there are many! From owl:Class to owl:FunctionalProperty, I review the terms that are essential and the ones you can wait till later to focus on.""" ;
	:cites :Source-f538e4c9-6803-54fd-9bf4-33edfc77312a ;	# The Open World Assumption
.

# pQqnEYRis4M · XSD Terms You Need to Know
:Source-32e86ab2-4e24-578a-874c-e10c03153b12 a :Video ;
	:name "XSD Terms You Need to Know" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT4M4S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2024-11-16"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2024-11-16T21:02:40-08:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained, :Source-22f2e7b2-fe8c-5c88-967e-c60d3167d172 ;	# Ontology Terms You NEED To Know
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pQqnEYRis4M"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """After covering the vocabulary you need from RDF, RDFS, and OWL, we still had a gap: we need to add numbers and dates and strings. To do this, XSD is essential. In this video, I cover the five most important XSD datatypes to get you off and running in building ontologies with OWL.

They are: integer, decimal, string (and language tags), date, and dateTime.""" ;
.

# VRxutB0zSxU · What is Artificial Intelligence? (I bet you don't know, either.)
:Source-b733e4f9-817e-508b-ad57-a8cbca147347 a :Video ;
	:name "What is Artificial Intelligence? (I bet you don't know, either.)" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT15M11S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2024-11-18"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2024-11-18T06:30:14-08:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained, :Source-83871c9d-6cd9-54ad-9c0a-76864f419c1a ;	# What is Artificial Intelligence?
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VRxutB0zSxU"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """This is a channel about ontology, philosophy, and artificial intelligence. So, I should be able to define AI cleanly, right? Well, this is embarrassing...I don't have a good definition for AI. In this video, I offer four potential definitions that I don't like. I'll dive into those in more depth in the future. The bulk of the video is explaining why it matters that we don't have a clear definition. To summarize:

1. Clarity Matters
2. \"AI\" is ubiquitous.
3. \"AI\" is used to drive governmental policies.
4. We should be wary of self-interested gatekeepers.
5. Unreflective use of AI may lead to the next AI Winter.

Join me on the upcoming videos as I embark on a quest to define AI. Or at least learn something trying to do so. It'll be fun!""" ;
.

# flm6m7TVmtA · Defining AI #1: Turing's Thinking Machines
:Source-b8670fa7-48ee-5f24-8e17-2f694c7294a5 a :Video ;
	:name "Defining AI #1: Turing's Thinking Machines" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT15M40S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2024-11-25"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2024-11-25T14:21:44-08:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained, :Source-83871c9d-6cd9-54ad-9c0a-76864f419c1a ;	# What is Artificial Intelligence?
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=flm6m7TVmtA"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """In the last video, I confessed that I don't have a tight definition for AI. I am now on a quest to remedy that, and we're starting with the popular Turing Test. Alan Turing's work in \"The Imitation Game\" is arguably the start of AI as we know it, and so it's a great place to snag our first definition: Artificial Intelligence is a thinking machine (as determined by the Turing Test).

Spoiler: This definition, while clear and influential, doesn't work. It fails to capture many things we intuitively think of as AI (e.g. Chat GPT and chess engines). And it has the fatal flaw that imitation is not identity.

I've got a few other definitions to try after this one, but I always want to hear what my viewers have to say.""" ;
	:cites :Source-a1193357-e432-5d77-8913-1348e01fa4c2 ;	# Computing Machinery and Intelligence
.

