# yE4pCdNcBlE · Synthetic Intelligence: Why Use "Artificial"?
:Source-6431687a-131f-525c-9aa6-8f8114309a6d a :Video ;
	:name "Synthetic Intelligence: Why Use \"Artificial\"?" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT9M56S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2025-08-22"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2025-08-22T00:00:57-07:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained ;
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yE4pCdNcBlE"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """Should we really call it “Artificial Intelligence”? In this video, I explore the language we use for AI — and how words like artificial, fake, synthetic, or counterfeit carry very different connotations. Marketers lean on “artificial” to make AI sound futuristic and impressive, but as consumers we should think carefully about what these terms imply.

If you’re interested in AI, language, or just cutting through the hype, this video is for you.""" ;
.

# B5vjnLy872c · Philosophy Explained: What is philosophy?
:Source-d83c87a4-89c2-52be-9004-85f623eb1d48 a :Video ;
	:name "Philosophy Explained: What is philosophy?" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT14M28S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2025-08-25"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2025-08-25T00:00:16-07:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained ;
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B5vjnLy872c"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """What is philosophy? I’m a philosopher, and in this video I explain what that means. Before diving into specific branches in future videos, I give a big-picture view of philosophy as a whole: what it covers, how it’s practiced, and why it matters.

My working definition: philosophy is the pursuit of truth through careful and clear thinking (with a little observation), especially as it has developed in the academic tradition.

By the end of this video, you’ll learn:

- What philosophy is (and isn’t)
- The major sub-disciplines of philosophy
- How to recognize a philosophical question or topic
- How you can start doing philosophy yourself""" ;
	:cites :Source-c91c62f8-01e8-54fd-950c-7b8b7e12c85f ,	# Philosophy for Beginners
		:Source-82837f62-b90c-59eb-a767-f1773cef79c4 ,	# What is Philosophy?: Crash Course Philosophy #1
		:Source-69332d10-0f38-52ff-8ebd-aa0efda2542e ,	# The Partially Examined Life (YouTube channel)
		:Source-83c107b4-8bfc-5ac8-93a1-cf4045a101cc ,	# Core Questions in Philosophy
		:Source-d97317ba-9ace-5038-8e89-1ad51085b5fa ,	# Symposium (Plato)
		:Source-427db4d5-68e3-5c5e-b637-e2cf66c1f63d ,	# Nicomachean Ethics (Aristotle)
		:Source-5be6c0c4-3502-58d4-a683-6c0a7441eafa ;	# Two Arguments for Intelligent Design | University Place
.

# phdsULAQSU4 · Defining AI #3: Haugeland's GOFAI (minds in the literal sense)
:Source-ef9bc195-76ee-5736-a8b6-5573609018a7 a :Video ;
	:name "Defining AI #3: Haugeland's GOFAI (minds in the literal sense)" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT19M50S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2025-08-27"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2025-08-27T18:18:18-07:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained, :Source-83871c9d-6cd9-54ad-9c0a-76864f419c1a ;	# What is Artificial Intelligence?
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=phdsULAQSU4"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """In this video, I unpack John Haugeland’s famous definition of “Good Old-Fashioned AI” (GOFAI) from his classic book AI: The Very Idea. Haugeland gives a philosophically rich account of artificial intelligence, one that captures the ambitions of AGI (Artificial General Intelligence) remarkably well.

But I argue that his definition falls short in two key ways:

1. It excludes nearly all of what we call AI today (machine learning, deep learning, etc.).
2. It doesn’t line up with what early AI practitioners like John McCarthy had in mind. In fact, Haugeland’s “AI” seems to be targeting something rather different from the field as it was practiced.

By the end of the video, you’ll see both the strengths and limits of Haugeland’s approach.""" ;
	:cites :Source-8e508954-b5ca-5abc-8236-fc07815998c6 ;	# Artificial Intelligence: The Very Idea
.

# N14EiKQvp-A · Logic Explained: The Philosophy of Arguments
:Source-4d0c7f39-6bc8-5086-b434-5bbc1704a1d6 a :Video ;
	:name "Logic Explained: The Philosophy of Arguments" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT25M25S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2025-08-29"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2025-08-29T16:45:35-07:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained, :Source-f4eb1cf9-0844-5435-b06b-68625e43c943 ;	# Logic and Inference
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N14EiKQvp-A"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """Arguments are more than just mere disagreement--they are how we establish reasons for things and justify our beliefs. And the study of building arguments is logic. In this (long!) video, I give an overview of logic. What is it? What are arguments? How can you find good ones? How can you become a logician? And what does this have to do with Artificial Intelligence? The answers to all these questions await!""" ;
	:cites :Source-1ef7f21a-da8b-54b1-ae63-2bdd3dd98fec ,	# Argument - Monty Python
		:Source-26a34c87-a68a-5412-932c-3be3568c6668 ,	# Beginning Logic
		:Source-5e6b8a3b-dfd0-5ada-b8f0-88c5db009347 ,	# The Logic Book
		:Source-1a0943a5-06e5-5d41-8e01-960c9fcfa009 ;	# The Power of Logic
.

# 8F8brEi-G24 · Let's Build a Chess Ontology (Part 1)
:Source-56c303e6-d6c3-55e0-a61d-2a2e1447070a a :Video ;
	:name "Let's Build a Chess Ontology (Part 1)" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT26M26S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2025-09-04"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2025-09-04T11:38:06-07:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
