# evUNPDnD14c · The Ad Hominem Fallacy: Distracting Attacks
:Source-16e362f5-4b96-5576-bba8-14d9b52eae77 a :Video ;
	:name "The Ad Hominem Fallacy: Distracting Attacks" ;
	:hasDuration [:duration "PT12M34S"^^xsd:duration] ;
	:releaseDate [:universalDate "2025-10-08"^^xsd:date ; :universalDateTime "2025-10-08T07:33:34-07:00"^^xsd:dateTime] ;
	:partOf :OntologyExplained, :Source-2893b7ee-72eb-5af3-818f-2005735c8dff ;	# Fallacies
	:createdBy :CaseyHart ;
	:url-Youtube "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=evUNPDnD14c"^^xsd:anyURI ;
	:description """“If they attack one personally, it means they have not a single political argument left.”  -- Margaret Thatcher

This video is a clear, practical guide to the ad hominem (literally “to the person”) fallacy — when an argument targets the person instead of the position. We'll define abusive and circumstantial forms, show when personal facts are legitimately relevant (character-as-subject, conflicts of interest, credibility), and walk through real-world examples and common misuses so you can spot and respond to these attacks.""" ;
.

# Rmcc5MOiQG0 · SPARQL Exploration: Querying Blind
